    "poweredBy": "Powered by Viator",
    "description": "This tour offers the perfect mix of land and water at New York City’s iconic attractions.\r\n\r\nOn the first part of the excursion, you’ll embark on a 30-minute guided walking tour of Battery Park – a public park named after the 17th-century artillery batteries built to protect the settlement behind. Afterwards, you’ll hop on board the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island ferry via reserve line access.\r\n\r\nThe ferry ride will take you to Liberty Island, where you can explore the Statue of Liberty. You’ll also have a chance to visit Ellis Island and see plenty of attractions along the way, including the SeaGlass Carousel, the Bosque Fountain and more.",
